sentences.t:
Hic subitam canibus rabiem Cocytia virgo
obicit et noto naris contingit odore,
ut cervum ardentes agerent;

sentences.l:
Here a sudden on the hounds madness the Cocytian maiden
throws, and with a known their nostrils touches scent,
so that the stag, burning, they should drive;

sentences.t:
Hic iuvenis primam ante aciem stridente sagitta,
natorum Tyrrhi fuerat qui maximus, Almo,
sternitur;

sentences.l:
Here a youth, before the first line, by a whistling arrow,
of the sons of Tyrrhus who had been the eldest, Almo,
is laid low;

sentences.t:
finitimas in bella feram rumoribus urbes
accendamque animos insani Martis amore,
undique ut auxilio veniunt;

sentences.l:
the neighbouring into wars I will bring with rumours, cities,
and I will kindle their spirits with love of mad Mars,
so that from all sides to help they may come;

sentences.t:
Te super aetherias errare licentius auras
haud pater ille velit, summi regnator Olympi:
cede locis;

sentences.l:
You above the upper to roam too freely airs
not would wish that father, of high the ruler Olympus:
withdraw from these places;

At once an accursed, all, against the omens, war,
against the fates of the gods, with perverse power, demand;
vying, the king's they surround house, Latinus's.
